From: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Force b_max=1 for all slots in legacy (SPL) init

SPL on sun50i-h5 uses the non-DM path (sunxi_mmc_init), not sunxi_mmc_probe().
CMD18 (multi-block read) desynchronizes the controller FIFO in PIO mode
on high-speed cards like eMMC and A2 microSD, so force single-block reads
(CMD17) for all slots in this path.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -690,6 +690,8 @@
 	if (mmc_resource_init(sdc_no) != 0)
 		return NULL;
 
+	cfg->b_max = 1;
+
 	/* config ahb clock */
 	debug("init mmc %d clock and io\n", sdc_no);
 #if !defined(CONFIG_SUN50I_GEN_H6) && !defined(CONFIG_SUNXI_GEN_NCAT2)
